--TEST--
A `///` run with no declaration under it is `E0127`, whether a blank line separates it from one or the file simply ends — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-attaches-to-the-next-declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-attaches-to-the-next-declaration`: a run documents
// the declaration under it across no blank line, so the blank line below is
// what makes this run document nothing.
/// A price, in the smallest unit its currency has.

final class Price {
    public const int MIN = 0;
}
echo Price::MIN, "\n";
// A run at the end of a file has no declaration under it at all, which is
// where the marker is most often a note written with one slash too many.
/// A note to whoever reads this next.
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0127]: this doc comment is attached to nothing
  --> %s:5:1
  |
5 | /// A price, in the smallest unit its currency has.
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ documents nothing
  = help: a doc comment documents the declaration it precedes, across no blank line; write `//` for a note to the reader

error[E0127]: this doc comment is attached to nothing
   --> %s:13:1
   |
13 | /// A note to whoever reads this next.
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ documents nothing
   = help: a doc comment documents the declaration it precedes, across no blank line; write `//` for a note to the reader

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
